  "scope": "The concrete repaired scalar trial has proved Gaussian strip bounds, a derived contour-shift identity, exponential Fourier decay and weighted Fourier square integrability for abs(hbar)<pi*epsilon. Its momentum modulations retain this integrability and have dense span in scalar clock L2. The same modulated family retains the earlier transverse derivative-energy condition after pullback. Full coupled L2 operator identification, all matter and charge-averaged energy terms, a dense full six-mode domain, capacity/regulator limits, physical identification and the TOE remain open. The strict parameter condition is sufficient for this proof; failure or necessity outside it is not claimed."
